@ ---- LBL :TONUM: the number of the text in X (digits and one point) to R49; "-": R49 = 0. Each character
@ is its place in "0123456789." (R35): a digit d: R43 = 10 R43 + d and R45 x R44 (R44 = 10 after the
@ point, 1 before); the point: R44 = 10. Then R43 / R45 ----
LBL 29
STO 34
0
STO 49
"-"
αPOS 34
X≥0?
RTN
0
STO 43
1
STO 44
STO 45
"0123456789."
STO 35
@ the text R34 character by character (until it is empty): a digit adds to the number (:DIGIT:), the point starts the decimals
DO 06
  αLENG 34
  X≠0?
WHILE 06
  1
  αLEFT 34
  αPOS 35
  10
  X=Y?
  STO 44
  X>Y?
  XEQ 30
  1
  αSL 34
ENDDO 06
RCL 43
RCL÷ 45
STO 49
RTN
@ LBL :DIGIT: one digit (X, 0-9) into the number R43 = 10 x R43 + X; after the point R45 counts the decimals
LBL 30
R↓
RCL 43
10
×
+
STO 43
RCL 44
STO× 45
RTN
